skill: "video-production-orchestrator"
sections[8]:
  - "\n"
  - "# AGYOS Video Production & Editing Orchestrator\n\nUnified production controller coordinating AGYOS video generation, headless clipping, talking-head editing, code-rendered shorts, mathematical animations, AI defect repair, organic film finishing, and post-render verification.\n\n"
  - "## 1. Route by Production Mode\n\nRun `bin/agyos video route \"<goal>\" --json` to inspect local capabilities and select the optimal pipeline:\n\n| Mode | Primary Skill & Tool | Best For |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Generative AI Cinema** | [google-flow](../google-flow/SKILL.md) + [veo-3](../veo-3/SKILL.md) | B-roll, product motion, multi-shot Scene Builder takes |\n| **Long-to-Short Clipping** | [chopify](../chopify/SKILL.md) (`./bin/chopify`) | Podcasts, VODs, URLs, livestreams -> 9:16 captioned clips |\n| **Talking-Head Editing** | [ai-video-editor](../ai-video-editor/SKILL.md) + `edl-render` | Pause/retake cuts, packed transcripts, motion graphics |\n| **Faceless Code Shorts** | [faceless-shorts-engine](../faceless-shorts-engine/SKILL.md) | Narrated 9:16 explainers rendered in headless browser + FFmpeg |\n| **Math & System Explainers** | [3b1b-manim](../3b1b-manim/SKILL.md) + [manim-video](../manim-video/SKILL.md) | Geometry, calculus, architecture diagrams, 9:16/16:9 Manim |\n| **Reference Style Transfer** | [taste-distillation](../taste-distillation/SKILL.md) + [taste-application](../taste-application/SKILL.md) | Measured 3D LUTs, shot cadence, EDL/FCPXML export |\n| **Long-Form YouTube** | [youtube-long-form-production](../youtube-long-form-production/SKILL.md) | 4-act retention scripts, B-roll cutaways, -14 LUFS masters |\n\n"
  - "## 2. The 12 Production-Correctness Hard Rules\n\n1. **Subtitles LAST**: Burn captions after all overlays and B-roll so graphics never cover text.\n2. **Per-Segment Extract -> Lossless Concat**: Extract and grade each EDL segment once, then `-c copy` concat.\n3. **30ms Boundary Audio Fades**: Apply `afade=t=in:st=0:d=0.03,afade=t=out:st={dur-0.03}:d=0.03` on every cut.\n4. **PTS-Shifted Overlays**: Apply `setpts=PTS-STARTPTS+T/TB` so overlay frame 0 aligns with its window start.\n5. **Output-Timeline SRT Remapping**: Compute `output_time = word.start - seg_start + seg_offset` via `edl-remap-srt`.\n6. **Word-Boundary Snapping**: Never cut inside a word; snap cut edges to verbatim word timestamps.\n7. **Cut Edge Padding**: Pad cut edges by 30-200ms (50ms pre / 80ms post default) to absorb ASR drift.\n8. **Packed Transcripts + On-Demand Visuals**: Pack word JSON into `takes_packed.md` (`pack-transcript`) and inspect cut boundaries with `timeline-view` instead of dumping raw frames.\n9. **De-AI Ordering Invariant**: Run structural repair (`deflicker`, `deband`, `vidstab`) BEFORE adding 35mm grain, halation, or Kodak 2383 LUTs.\n10. **Aspect-Preserving Motion**: Preserve exact input dimensions (`iw:ih`) during handheld drift across 9:16, 16:9, and 1:1.\n11. **Measured Loudness Mastering**: Normalize to `-14 LUFS / -1.0 dBTP` (two-pass `loudnorm`) and verify with `ebur128`.\n12. **Post-Render Self-Eval Gate**: Run `self-eval` (`ffprobe`, `ebur128`, `blackdetect`) and inspect cut-boundary filmstrips before delivery (max 3 fix iterations).\n\n"
  - "## 3. Standard Agentic Editing Pipeline\n\n```text\n1. Intake & Probe     -> ffprobe every source; confirm aspect, fps, audio, and user strategy\n2. Transcribe & Pack  -> bin/agyos video pack-transcript transcript.json --out takes_packed.md\n3. Plan & Validate    -> Draft edl.json; run bin/agyos video edl-validate edl.json --check-files\n4. Remap Captions     -> bin/agyos video edl-remap-srt edl.json transcript.json --out master.srt\n5. Render & Finish    -> bin/agyos video edl-render edl.json -o preview.mp4 --preview\n6. Self-Eval & Critic -> bin/agyos video self-eval preview.mp4 --edl edl.json --json\n                         bin/agyos video timeline-view preview.mp4 <t-1.5> <t+1.5> -o cut_check.png\n7. Final Master       -> bin/agyos video edl-render edl.json -o final.mp4\n```\n\n"
  - "## 4. Generative AI Cinema Pipeline (Google Flow -> De-AI Master)\n\n1. Draft a 5-part Veo 3.1 prompt: `bin/agyos video veo-prompt \"<idea>\" --ratio 9:16 --duration 8 --json`.\n2. Dry-run in Google Flow (`auto_confirm: false`), inspect screenshot, then generate (`auto_confirm: true`).\n3. Extend long takes via Scene Builder 7-second hops (`flow_scene_add` -> `flow_scene_extend`), restating subject, wardrobe, lighting, and camera move in every hop.\n4. Remove corner watermark: `uv run scripts/remove_flow_watermark.py raw.mp4 delogo.mp4`.\n5. Repair temporal/compression defects: `uv run scripts/repair_ai_video.py full delogo.mp4 -o repaired.mp4`.\n6. Apply organic cinema finish: `uv run scripts/organic_film_engine.py master repaired.mp4 -o final.mp4 --profile cinema-2383`.\n7. Verify with `bin/agyos video self-eval final.mp4 --json`.\n\n"
  - "## 5. Editorial & Psychological Standards\n\n- **Walter Murch Rule of Six**: Prioritize Emotion (51%), Story (23%), and Rhythm (10%) over mechanical continuity ([video-editing-principles](../video-editing-principles/SKILL.md)).\n- **Vertical Safe Zones**: Keep critical text and subjects inside the central `1080x1400` window (200px top, 320px bottom clear) and audit scripts with `bin/agyos video audit <script.md>` ([vertical-video-psychology](../vertical-video-psychology/SKILL.md)).\n- **Forensic & Disclosure Integrity**: Never strip SynthID or C2PA provenance; disclose synthetic media per platform rules ([ai-video-detection-forensics](../ai-video-detection-forensics/SKILL.md)).\n\n"
  - "## 6. AGYOS Governance & Execution Rules\n\n- Confirm strategy, cut plans, and credit-spending generations with the user before execution.\n- Never publish, upload, or schedule finished videos without separate explicit authorization.\n- In the AGYOS repository itself, run tests, builds, and media renders only via GitHub Actions CI; execute local media workflows only in user-approved project directories.\n"
